zoox,2025-06,68653,309922,235760,444401,54809,82497,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est., rebuilt 2026-10-03: central = the month's California driverless miles from the CA DMV Dec 2024-Nov 2025 driverless mileage report (Zoox permit AVDT004; Jun-Nov 2025: 22,508 / 26,630 / 36,072 / 35,017 / 42,286 / 56,275 mi) + a Las Vegas share. The LV share is what remains of Zoox's official ~1.3M driverless miles as of Dec 31, 2025 (letter to NHTSA Jan 28, 2026, docket NHTSA-2025-0523-0004 p.22) after the 40,080 pre-series miles, CA and the May 2024-May 2025 rows, kept in the shape of the pre-rebuild estimate scaled by 0.879 (Jun-Dec 2025: 46,145 / 60,104 / 73,780 / 101,080 / 124,579 / 148,324 / 197,373 mi); that puts the 1M-mile crossing (pre-series miles included) around Nov 22, matching Fortune's Dec 17, 2025 report that the fleet 'passed its 1-million-mile technical benchmark' 'a few weeks ago', and Las Vegas past ~350k by Sep 10, 2025, when Zoox's CTO told the Las Vegas Review-Journal the robotaxis had driven 'many of hundreds of thousands of miles here in Las Vegas'. Band = CA + 0.7x-1.3x the LV share. Free rides only (paid LV blocked pending the FMVSS exemption, eventually granted Jul 30, 2026)."
