zoox,2025-12,245852,1259920,1190013,1319873,174642,317387,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est., rebuilt 2026-10-03: cumulative = Zoox's official ~1.3M driverless miles as of Dec 31, 2025 (letter to NHTSA Jan 28, 2026, docket NHTSA-2025-0523-0004 p.22) less the 40,080 pre-series miles (CA DMV Feb 2023-Apr 2024 + an equal-to-CA Las Vegas analog) = 1,259,920. California's December is not yet in any published DMV report (it falls in the Dec 2025-Nov 2026 reporting year): est. 48,480 mi = the DMV November 56,275 x the CPUC pilot Dec/Nov ratio (36,482 / 42,347 mi), floored at the CPUC 36,482 (pilot miles are a subset of DMV driverless miles) and capped at 60,803 (pilot share 60%); Las Vegas share 197,373 mi (band 0.7x-1.3x), the last step of the Jun-Dec 2025 ramp. Cumulative band (knot added 2026-10-03): 1,190,013 to 1,319,873, the disclosure's own uncertainty rather than the running sum of the monthly bands: 'approximately 1.3 million' read as its rounding interval, 1.25M-1.35M, less the pre-series miles at their own band (California's 20,174 measured, the Las Vegas analog at 0.5x-2x of 19,906: 30,127 to 59,987). Later months' bands chain forward from it, and Oct-Nov 2025's are narrowed back from it. Free rides only (paid LV blocked pending the FMVSS exemption, eventually granted Jul 30, 2026)."
