waymo,2025-02,6855760,63405761,61389702,65421820,5141819,8569701,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est.: CA CPUC driverless VMT scaled to US via cumulative milestone intervals (IGNOREME.md, Waymo VMT Methodology). Cumulative anchors (re-chained 2026-08-28, monthly shape within each anchor interval unchanged): the Waymo Safety Impact hub's All-Locations total plus an estimate of rider-only miles in metros the hub had not yet benchmarked, less ~0.15M pre-series miles: 71.47M end-Mar-2025 (hub 71.432M + 0.188M), 96.52M end-Jun-2025 (95.965M + 0.7M) and 129.01M end-Sep-2025 (127.158M + 2.0M) (data/README.md, Waymo anchors). The earlier published milestones (9.3M end-2023 to 56.7M Jan-2025) are exact centrals minus ~0.15M pre-series miles, not floors. Since 2026-10-04 the cumulative band at the Mar-2025 and Jun-2025 anchors is the anchor's own uncertainty, as at Sep-2025 through Jun-2026: the hub total plus the excluded miles, less 0.15M, which is 71,470,000 with no spread at Mar-2025 (the Atlanta and Mountain View miles the hub lists are exact) and 96,215,000 to 97,115,000 at Jun-2025 (the low and high unbenchmarked-metro estimates, 0.4M to 1.3M); the Feb, Apr and May 2025 bands are chained from the two (the two anchor bands had sat 4% and 2.5% either side)."
