waymo,2026-01,16034802,190296802,185588102,195205502,12026102,20043502,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est.: calibrated to Waymo's 220.6M rider-only miles through Mar 2026 (Safety Impact hub, Jun 24, 2026 update), bridging the 174.26M end-Dec-2025 anchor to the 222.46M end-Mar-2026 anchor (the hub's 220.613M plus 2.0M estimated in metros the hub had not yet benchmarked, less ~0.15M pre-series miles; data/README.md, Waymo anchors); consistent with >4M mi/week late Mar; CPUC Q1-2026 CA driverless actuals 9.09M Jan/8.19M Feb/9.11M Mar (54.9% CA share after the 2026-08-28 re-chain) corroborate level and shape within ~4%; ±25%. Re-chained 2026-08-28 with the monthly shape within each anchor interval unchanged."
tesla,2026-02,324000,1279000,1240630,1470850,275400,405000,1,1,1,1,1,1,"Tesla's own Cumulative Paid Robotaxi Miles chart: monthly values vector-extracted from the Q4-2025 and Q1-2026 update-deck PDFs (overlapping months agree within ~3k mi; 658k end-2025, 1.717M end-Mar-2026). Texas driverless service only — the Q3-2025 call tracks Bay Area as a separate supervised series (1M+ mi by Oct 2025) and Aug-2025's ~13k delta is too small to contain the Bay fleet. Read as fleet service miles incl. deadhead, matching the incident scope (None + In-Vehicle + Remote Commercial/Test); if 'paid' is literally passenger-on-board miles the true total is higher, so the cumulative band's top carries ~15% upside and its floor ~3% read noise."
