waymo,2026-03,17097348,222463000,221663000,223763000,12823011,21371685,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est.: calibrated to Waymo's 220.6M rider-only miles through Mar 2026 (Safety Impact hub, Jun 24, 2026 update; per-city cumulative PHX 80.6M, SF 67.1M, LA 51.8M, ATX 15.8M, ATL 5.4M): lands on the 222.46M end-Mar-2026 anchor (the hub's 220.613M plus 2.0M estimated in metros the hub had not yet benchmarked, less ~0.15M pre-series miles; data/README.md, Waymo anchors); CPUC Q1-2026 CA driverless actuals 9.09M Jan/8.19M Feb/9.11M Mar (54.9% CA share after the 2026-08-28 re-chain) corroborate level and shape within ~4%; ±25%. Re-chained 2026-08-28 with the monthly shape within each anchor interval unchanged."
tesla,2026-04,374000,2091000,2028270,2404650,317900,467500,1,1,1,1,1,1,"Tesla's own Cumulative Paid Robotaxi Miles chart: monthly values vector-extracted from the Q2-2026 update-deck PDF (13 points through Jun-2026, 2.440M end-Q2; overlapping months re-confirm the earlier decks' series within ~8k mi). Austin + Dallas/Houston (unsupervised Dallas/Houston launch Apr 18, 2026); Bay Area remains a separate supervised series. Read as fleet service miles incl. deadhead, matching the incident scope (None + In-Vehicle + Remote Commercial/Test); if 'paid' is literally passenger-on-board miles the true total is higher, so the cumulative band's top carries ~15% upside and its floor ~3% read noise. (Pre-pin activity-ratio estimates ran ~1.4-2.9x high for Q2's months, +28% on the end-Q2 cumulative — a utilization-led slowdown the fleet counts missed.)"
waymo,2026-04,18025220,240488220,238176464,243749976,16513464,19986976,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est., bottom-up on the Waymo hub's MEASURED Q2 (Sep 24, 2026 update: 271.329M rider-only miles thru Jun-2026; re-chained 2026-09-25): CA = CPUC Q2-2026 driverless actual 9,414,525 deployment + 51,198 pilot (CPUC's total driverless VMT incl. deadhead) x 1.0576, the hub-vs-CPUC ratio for the hub's CA counties in Q2 (Q1: 1.040) = 10.01M (±3%); Maricopa 3.87M and Travis 1.72M = the hub's measured Q2 county increments (11.57M / 5.28M) split by the prior monthly shape (±10%); Atlanta 1.02M = the hub's measured Q2 Fulton+DeKalb increment (3.25M) split by the prior monthly shape (±10%); + rider-only metros the hub does not count (Miami, Dallas, Houston, Orlando, Nashville; San Antonio passenger service halted Apr 20 to Sep 17 after flood strandings Apr 4 and Apr 20) 1.40M [0.85M, 2.40M]. Miami/Orlando open to all Apr 15; Nashville public Apr 7. The Jun-2026 cumulative lands on the anchor: the hub's 271.329M plus 6.65M estimated in metros the hub does not count, less ~0.15M pre-series miles (data/README.md, Waymo anchors)."
