waymo,2026-05,18514196,259002416,255160284,264287794,16983820,20544572,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est., bottom-up on the Waymo hub's MEASURED Q2 (Sep 24, 2026 update: 271.329M rider-only miles thru Jun-2026; re-chained 2026-09-25): CA = CPUC Q2-2026 driverless actual 9,704,968 deployment + 102,205 pilot (CPUC's total driverless VMT incl. deadhead) x 1.0576, the hub-vs-CPUC ratio for the hub's CA counties in Q2 (Q1: 1.040) = 10.37M (±3%); Maricopa 3.92M and Travis 1.72M = the hub's measured Q2 county increments (11.57M / 5.28M) split by the prior monthly shape (±10%); Atlanta 1.05M = the hub's measured Q2 Fulton+DeKalb increment (3.25M) split by the prior monthly shape (±10%); + rider-only metros the hub does not count (Miami, Dallas, Houston, Orlando, Nashville; San Antonio passenger service halted Apr 20 to Sep 17 after flood strandings Apr 4 and Apr 20) 1.45M [0.90M, 2.50M]. ALL US freeway rides suspended from May 21 (construction-zone/flood software fixes); TX/Atlanta/Nashville weather pause ~May 20-28; Miami +50 sq mi May 13. The Jun-2026 cumulative lands on the anchor: the hub's 271.329M plus 6.65M estimated in metros the hub does not count, less ~0.15M pre-series miles (data/README.md, Waymo anchors)."
